Q: manifest icons Line 1 not , column: 1, Unexpected token A: <p>It's because the browser does not understand the MIME type of the manifest file and thus cannot find it. In Chrome DevTools > Network > Headers > Content-Type, the content-type of the manifest must match the actual manifest file extension (<code>.json</code> or <code>.webmanifest</code>).</p>

<p>In ASP.NET, you need to declare the file type in <code>web.config</code>:</p>

<pre><code>&lt;staticContent&gt;
  &lt;mimeMap fileExtension=".json" mimeType="application/json" /&gt;
  &lt;mimeMap fileExtension=".webmanifest" mimeType="application/manifest+json" /&gt;
&lt;/staticContent&gt;
</code></pre>
